{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets the maximum number of samples to take when using anisotropic filtering on textures (as a power of two). A higher sample count will result in sharper textures at oblique angles, but is more expensive to compute. A value of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":" forcibly disables anisotropic filtering, even on materials where it is enabled."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"viewportSetAnisotropicFilteringLevel","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"viewport","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RID","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiftGodotRuntime3RIDC"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"anisotropicFilteringLevel","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RenderingServer","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RenderingServer","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot15RenderingServerC"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"ViewportAnisotropicFiltering","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RenderingServer\/ViewportAnisotropicFiltering","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot15RenderingServerC28ViewportAnisotropicFilteringO"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The anisotropic filtering level also affects decals and light projectors if they are configured to use anisotropic filtering. See "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProjectSettings\/rendering\/textures\/decals\/filter"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProjectSettings\/rendering\/textures\/lightProje